ation-break property working on inline elements.\n       Display the highlighted elements as inline-block as a workaround.\n       https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=682173\n\n       The set of selectors is purposefully kept small and simple. It\'s unlikely that WYSIWYG content would use more\n       complex elements so lets avoid being too eager. They\'re purposefull kept simple as this is used in the context\n       of Ally for Web and we want to make sure we\'re not overriding any other display rules that might be set by\n       more specific rules applied by the client. */\n    display: inline-block;\n    box-decoration-break: clone !important;\n    line-height: calc(100% + 12px) !important;\n    padding-left: 2px;\n    padding-right: 2px;\n    position: relative !important;\n}\n\na[data-ally-html-preview-highlight] {\n    max-width: calc(100% - 13px);\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-highlight-shadow] {\n    position: relative;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n    width: fit-content;\n    height: fit-content;\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-highlight-shadow]::before {\n    content: "";\n    position: absolute;\n    top: -6px;\n    left: -6px;\n    right: -6px;\n    bottom: -6px;\n    background:\n        repeating-linear-gradient(\n            -45deg,\n            #AF0216,\n            #AF0216 3px,\n            #FF919E 2px,\n            #FF919E 5px\n        );\n    z-index: -1;\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-highlight],\n[data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset]::after,\n[data-ally-html-preview-outline-outset]::after {\n    border: double 6px #AF0216 !important;\n    border-image:\n        repeating-linear-gradient(\n            -45deg,\n            #AF0216,\n            #AF0216 3px,\n            #FF919E 2px,\n            #FF919E 5px\n        ) 5 !important;\n    scroll-margin: 50px !important;\n    scroll-padding: 50px !important;\n    box-sizing: content-box !important;\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset] {\n    position: relative !important;\n    background: none !important;\n    padding: 8px !important;\n}\n\n/* Atto overrides z-index in a weird way that only 0 index needs to be used as an underlay. */\n.ally-wysiwyg-feedback-atto-fullscreen [data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset],\n.ally-wysiwyg-feedback-atto-fullscreen [data-ally-html-preview-outline-outset] {\n    z-index: 0;\n}\n\n/* Atto tables doesn\'t expand cell child elements, removing correct hover cursor on cells. */\n.ally-wysiwyg-feedback-atto-fullscreen th[data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset] > span,\n.ally-wysiwyg-feedback-atto-fullscreen td[data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset] > span {\n    display: inline-block;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-outline-outset] {\n    position: relative !important;\n    margin: 8px !important;\n    max-width: calc(100% - 16px) !important;\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset]::after {\n    content: \'\';\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 0;\n    left: 0;\n    right: 0;\n    bottom: 0;\n    z-index: -1;\n}\n\n[data-ally-html-preview-outline-outset]::after {\n    content: \'\';\n    position: absolute;\n    top: -6px;\n    left: -6px;\n    right: -6px;\n    bottom: -6px;\n    z-index: -1;\n}\n\n/* AY-5910: TinyMCE adds an empty line-break when inserting text into or blanking out table headers. Combined with\n   Ally\'s ::after content elements, this causes the cell to grow and creates a janky effect.\n   Avoid this by forcing the line-height to 0 which will enforce the smallest possible line. As soon as the user starts\n   typing, TinyMCE\'s line-break will be ignored due to the line-height. This is obviously problematic when the line in\n   the cell needs to wrap. However, given the feedback check is fairly quick, the issue should be resolved after having\n   typed a few characters. That will remove the outline and alleviate the need for this workaround. */\ntable th[data-ally-html-preview-outline-inset] {\n    line-height: 0;\n}\n'},3994:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";n.d(t,{f:()=>i});va